{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00918",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.81,
      "end_seconds": 13.9,
      "duration_seconds": 11.09,
      "text": "Hi there! I get these terrible headaches every spring, always around the same time, and I've finally decided to ask someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.9,
      "end_seconds": 23.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "I'm glad you did. Tell me what they feel like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.99,
      "end_seconds": 34.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.68,
      "text": "Like a hot poker behind my right eye. It's the worst pain I've ever had, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.84,
      "end_seconds": 42.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "How long does an attack last?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.33,
      "end_seconds": 50.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "About an hour, sometimes 90 minutes. Then it goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.52,
      "end_seconds": 56.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "How many times a day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.42,
      "end_seconds": 66.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "Two or three, and often at night. It wakes me up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.86,
      "end_seconds": 76.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "How long does the run of headaches go on for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.66,
      "end_seconds": 83.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Six weeks or so, then they just stop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.53,
      "end_seconds": 93.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "Any watering of the eye, or a blocked nose on that side during the attack?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.63,
      "end_seconds": 107.95,
      "duration_seconds": 10.32,
      "text": "Yes! The eye waters like a tap, and my nose runs on the right side. How did you know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.1,
      "end_seconds": 120.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "That's a very typical pattern. Do you stay still or pace about during an attack? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.59,
      "end_seconds": 129.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "I can't sit still. I pace up and down. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.18,
      "end_seconds": 138.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "That's also typical. Any nausea, or flashing lights before it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.51,
      "end_seconds": 145.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "No. Nothing like that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.72,
      "end_seconds": 157.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "Have you had any head injury, or any weakness, or any change in your vision between attacks? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.9,
      "end_seconds": 166.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "None of that, no. I'm perfectly well in between. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.15,
      "end_seconds": 175.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "And is there a family history of migraine or headaches? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.5,
      "end_seconds": 186.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "My uncle had something like it, I think. But I don't really know. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.97,
      "end_seconds": 198.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "This sounds like cluster headache, which comes in runs, often in the same season each year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.94,
      "end_seconds": 206.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Is it serious? Is it a tumour? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.17,
      "end_seconds": 220.63,
      "duration_seconds": 11.46,
      "text": "Cluster headache is painful but not dangerous in itself. Because your story is so typical, I wouldn't expect a scan to show anything. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.01,
      "end_seconds": 227.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "That's a relief. Is there treatment? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.56,
      "end_seconds": 245.45,
      "duration_seconds": 14.89,
      "text": "Yes. There are treatments for stopping an attack, and ones for preventing the run. I'd like to refer you to a neurologist to plan it properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.61,
      "end_seconds": 251.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "That makes sense. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.35,
      "end_seconds": 262.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "I'll write the referral letter today, and the neurology team will contact you directly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.48,
      "end_seconds": 268.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Good, thank you. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.2,
      "end_seconds": 278.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Meanwhile, avoid alcohol during a run, as it can set off an attack."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.75,
      "end_seconds": 286.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Yes, that's true, now you say it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.2,
      "end_seconds": 298.06,
      "duration_seconds": 8.86,
      "text": "If the pain changes, or you get weakness, confusion or a stiff neck, come in at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.63,
      "end_seconds": 305.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "I will. Thank you so much. ~"
    }
  ]
}
